{
    /* π by Monte Carlo, with `?`, the roll without state.

       Every cell hashes its own seed — its coordinates plus INPUT, which the
       caller fills with a number that changes from call to call — into two
       coordinates in [0, 1), and asks whether the point falls inside the
       quarter circle. `◇+1` counts the hits along each row; the caller sums
       the 256 rows and multiplies by 4 / 65536.

       A roll is the same on every thread and every run, so the estimate is
       reproducible for a given INPUT, and a different INPUT is a different
       sample.

         rhoc examples/montecarlo.rho
    */
    INPUT:◯ □ 256 256

    (((⍳0 INPUT) × 256.0) + (⍳1 INPUT) + INPUT) → SEED
    (?SEED) → U
    (?(SEED + 0.5)) → V
    (ind (((U × U) + (V × V)) < 1.0)) → HIT
    (◇+1 HIT) → =
}
